WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.380
Let's create a button band
with a beautiful edge finish.

2
00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.500
This method can use any
needle arrangement.

3
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:13.180
I chose to knit my band
in full needle rib.

4
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.660
Knit the band separately with a nice

5
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:21.860
tubular cast on and then attach
it to the front garment edge.

6
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.580
Start by establishing the number

7
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:30.500
of needles needed for your edge.
Cast on using the method of your choice.

8
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:35.300
I'm using my favorite Broken Toe Cast On.

9
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.700
Once the cast on is complete,
set up for the needle arrangement of your

10
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:45.800
choice and knit the number
of rows for your band.

11
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.820
Transfer all the stitches up
to the main bed and knit one row.

12
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.020
Knit a row of ravel cord and scrap off.

13
00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:03.020
Now set that band aside
and with the right side facing,

14
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:09.120
rehang the garment edge,
pushing it back behind the latches.

15
00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:15.490
Next, pick up the band stitches with
the wrong side of the band facing you.

16
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.620
Place these stitches
in the hooks of the needles.

17
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.820
When all the stitches are on the machine,
close the latches and pull the band

18
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:33.480
stitches through the garment edge
and loosely bind off.

19
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.260
This bind off is a bit bulky.

20
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:42.040
You may want to use a sewn or
a backstitch bind off instead.

21
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.380
By knitting the band separately,

22
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:50.760
we can take advantage of that beautiful
cast on edge for the edge of our band.

